From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: jail: let aarch64 device processes read their thread name

Every aarch64 device policy allowed prctl(PR_SET_NAME) only. A device
process that reads its own name with PR_GET_NAME (as a fault reporter
does before it prints where a fault happened) was killed by seccomp, so a
SIGBUS showed up as "Bad system call". Allow PR_GET_NAME next to
PR_SET_NAME in every aarch64 policy that allows prctl, as the runtime VMM
does. It only reads the calling thread's own name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
